   image gate: kimball_house_1801_prairie taylor_c1895_northwest: verdict "differs", 11 difference(s) open: both loggia arches, and their carving with them, render about 15-20 px south (the front's, x 1025-1105 against the print's 1010-1080) and east (the 18th Street face's, its corner pier at x 980-995 against the print's 955-974) of the print's; the south pavilion's south corner renders about 28 px south of the print's (x 1368 against 1335-1340) and its gable's apex about 30 px (x 1300 against 1270): the 1911 sheet draws the pavilion's south-west corner chamfered about 0.45 m back to the south wall behind the front's plane, where the build stands it square; the frieze over the pavilion's third-storey pair: a dressed band with a roundel on the pair's axis (about y 430-470 on the print) under the shelf the gable springs from; the build's wall there is plain; the tower's form: a shaft about 2.4 m across under a corbelled upper stage about 3.6 m across, its cone flaring from the stage; the build is one eight-sided prism 2.9 m across; the gabled section on the flank: a gable facing 18th Street with a balcony at about 11.5 m; the build has a hip there; the south pavilion's gable is filled with a carved panel, a tall leafy relief up the tympanum to the apex; the build's gable face is plain stone; the main cornice: a heavy moulded stone cornice under the roof's faces; the build's eave is K05's plain fascia and soffit (K10's moulded stone cornice stands only under a flat or gable roof); the flank section stands about 0.1 m proud on the sheet; the build stands it 0.6 m proud (K08's pavilion depth, the least its window recesses fit in; the main eave's gutter, its lip 0.46 m out, also dies behind it), and 6.0 m wide (K08's widest) against the photograph's about 7.8 m, short of the gabled section. The pavilion stood 0.6 m proud too; the east turret's shaft and finial: the print shows the shaft about 15 px wider toward the front (to x 237; the build's to about x 220), a moulded band at its first floor and a heavy eave moulding, and a finial spike about 40 px taller than the build's; the mansard's curb and deck: at the front's north-west corner the print's curb stands about 35-50 px lower than the build's (the corner hip's top at about x 950, y 320 against 978, 247) and its corner hip runs about 25-30 px west of the build's; the front's deck ends at the print's x 1092 under its south finial, where the build's runs on to x 1187. So the cresting, the corner hood and its finial stand about 35-50 px over the print's, and the south finial about 95 px south of it (seen by T-3000); the hooded dormers' hoods: the print's cheeks widen further up the roof than the build's (the flank's lit cheek about 45 px across at the top against the build's about 25), as its lower faces fall back faster than the build's 72 degrees do; and their faces are slate with a pale frame round the light, where the build's are stone
